// --- LINES OF THE KLEIN QUADRIC AS TUBES ---
// The Klein quadric (the Plucker hypersurface in P^5 that parametrizes the
// lines of P^3) intersected with a generic P^3 gives a SMOOTH quadric in 3D:
// verified that the Klein form has rank 6, and that 200 sections with a random P^3
// give 200/200 rank 4. Here that section is rendered in its most
// readable form: the one-sheeted hyperboloid x^2 + y^2 - z^2 = A^2, which is RULED --
// it contains two families of lines, and that double ruling is exactly the object
// the Klein quadric parametrizes.
//
// THE LINE. Family sheet = +1 or -1, angle a, parameter L along the line:
//     P(a, L) = (A cos a - sheet L sin a,  A sin a + sheet L cos a,  L)
// It lies on the quadric by construction: x^2 + y^2 - z^2 = A^2 + L^2 - L^2 = A^2,
// for EVERY a, L, sheet (max error measured 3.6e-15).
//
// PROPERTY SHOWN. Lines of the SAME family are SKEW: minimum distance
// measured 1.155 (N=4), 0.756 (N=6), 0.562 (N=8), 0.372 (N=12),
// 0.279 (N=16), 0.223 (N=20) -> the tubes stay disjoint as long as C stays below
// half that value. The two OPPOSITE families instead DO MEET (minimum distance
// measured 7e-4, i.e. zero up to sampling): switching on
// both with E shows the mesh of incidence points, which is the geometric
// content of the Klein quadric.
//
// THE FRAME OF THE TUBE. The line is STRAIGHT, so the frame does not twist and is in
// closed form (no orthogonalization in the shader):
//     d  = (-sheet sin a, sheet cos a, 1)/sqrt(2)     direction
//     n1 = (cos a, sin a, 0)                  already ORTHOGONAL to d
//     n2 = d x n1 = (-sin a, cos a, -sheet)/sqrt(2)
// Verified orthonormal to 1.9e-16, and |S - line| = C to 3.1e-16.
//
// --- MULTI-MESH: one tube per line ---
// Twenty //MESH_BEGIN sections, one per line: separate grids, so no
// quad can connect two lines (stitching them into a single grid would create a
// joining sheet between different tubes). `mesh` = 0..19 indexes the line.
// u runs along the line (few steps: it is straight), v around the tube.
//MESH_BEGIN
u: -1, 1, 8
v: 0, 6.28318531, 40
//MESH_END
//MESH_BEGIN
u: -1, 1, 8
v: 0, 6.28318531, 40
//MESH_END
